                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Vibrantly, vividly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bc162032-3192-3ae3-b3bc-08903228c7e1",
                                        "entry_id": "146db809-ee9a-3859-a33c-d4d01e08c12d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a lifelike manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba2bc41e-6590-4930-bd87-308b134c0878",
                                                "sense_id": "bc162032-3192-3ae3-b3bc-08903228c7e1",
                                                "text": "Him to a dainty flowre she did transmew, / Which in that cloth was wrought, as if it liuely grew."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ac9f5433-0a35-4ee9-93f7-dc6cbb60b0db",
                                                "sense_id": "bc162032-3192-3ae3-b3bc-08903228c7e1",
                                                "text": "the Painter Protogenes […] having perfected the image of a wearie and panting dog, […] but being unable, as he desired, lively to represent the drivel or slaver of his mouth, vexed against his owne worke, took his spunge, and moist as it was with divers colours, threw it at the picture […]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "070b1d4a-6dac-49b1-b6a8-859039e20e23",
                        "source_entry_id": "b72fb7ae-3e08-3d8b-b324-a7901033dd18",
                        "target_lang_word": "merrily",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "merrily",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8fdb002a-6d33-312d-a758-dce7c0bec2c5",
                                        "entry_id": "4320378a-29f8-361a-a4eb-326edb55c71e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a cheerful or merry way."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ab30789-b84c-4a8f-a9a0-68943b899c72",
                                                "sense_id": "8fdb002a-6d33-312d-a758-dce7c0bec2c5",
                                                "text": "So quickly the poore mans ſubſtance is ſpent,\nBut merrily with the world it went,\nVVhen men eat berries of the hauthorne tree, […]\nAnd old men knew not vſurie:\nNow tis come to a wofull paſſe, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "03ccccb1-b07b-47b7-82e1-83a44ca81c2c",
                                                "sense_id": "8fdb002a-6d33-312d-a758-dce7c0bec2c5",
                                                "text": "Ariell:\nWhere the Bee ſucks, there ſuck I,\nIn a Cowslips bell, I lie,\nThere I cowch when Owles doe crie,\nOn the Batts backe I doe flie\n  after Sommer merrily.\nMerrily, merrily, ſhall I liue now\nVnder the bloſſom that hangs on the Bow."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "63977960-5cfa-46e1-bfce-2792105a371d",
                                                "sense_id": "8fdb002a-6d33-312d-a758-dce7c0bec2c5",
                                                "text": "Then Heidi would sit down and chatter merrily away."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "90481697-c10c-4d02-8de1-1210a3309ed9",
                        "source_entry_id": "b72fb7ae-3e08-3d8b-b324-a7901033dd18",
                        "target_lang_word": "happily",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "happily",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "de95d93e-c960-3e47-a541-aaa00b2e88ea",
                                        "entry_id": "71bd1161-03d3-3c86-8e05-e53c2b9a8d5a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a happy or cheerful manner; with happiness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f0cd391-bf2c-4c06-a226-f5f6ee3ea0b1",
                                                "sense_id": "de95d93e-c960-3e47-a541-aaa00b2e88ea",
                                                "text": "This time next month I’ll be happily fishing at the beach."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aa828e31-617b-450e-8739-5baf0be85ba0",
                                                "sense_id": "de95d93e-c960-3e47-a541-aaa00b2e88ea",
                                                "text": "And thus I have given the first part of a life of fortune and adventure, a life of Providence's chequer-work, and of a variety which the world will seldom be able to shew the like of: beginning foolishly, but closing much more happily than any part of it ever gave me leave so much as to hope for."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea2ce3e6-936d-43e7-a3de-784a79335de4",
                                                "sense_id": "de95d93e-c960-3e47-a541-aaa00b2e88ea",
                                                "text": "Train operating companies get plenty of column inches in the tabloids, usually for negative reasons. Happily, Southeastern is worthy of praise for having made The Sun for something positive."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "81054a6c-9a4e-3d16-8f60-660610a36c31",
                                        "entry_id": "71bd1161-03d3-3c86-8e05-e53c2b9a8d5a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "By good chance; fortunately, successfully."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "774e1733-253b-494b-a480-193607f08318",
                                                "sense_id": "81054a6c-9a4e-3d16-8f60-660610a36c31",
                                                "text": "Watt wore, on his feet, a boot, brown in colour, and a shoe, happily of a brownish colour also."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9ad5cb87-5a0a-3781-a61e-31639014727b",
                                        "entry_id": "71bd1161-03d3-3c86-8e05-e53c2b9a8d5a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "With good will; in all happiness; willingly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "62a17171-6d89-4412-9f16-b5f172348077",
                                                "sense_id": "9ad5cb87-5a0a-3781-a61e-31639014727b",
                                                "text": "I will happily help you look for your lost wallet."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f5306604-7dff-3488-9c86-f35980b59732",
                                        "entry_id": "71bd1161-03d3-3c86-8e05-e53c2b9a8d5a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "By chance; perhaps."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "72740378-37da-4b13-be3e-540bafc6c561",
                                                "sense_id": "f5306604-7dff-3488-9c86-f35980b59732",
                                                "text": "And who knoweth whether a thousand yeares hence a third opinion will rise, which happily shall overthrow these two precedents?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "683ea3e5-a402-46b7-9980-2a85ce460e20",
                        "source_entry_id": "b72fb7ae-3e08-3d8b-b324-a7901033dd18",
                        "target_lang_word": "gayly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "gayly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2629098b-3fd1-32a3-af57-604cd524dcbf",
                                        "entry_id": "128070e0-fe1c-3a02-a4b9-319dc5bbe08d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Cheerfully; in a gay manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated",
                                            "uncommon"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d7ab63df-88e6-4ed5-83ea-942428aeb621",
                                                "sense_id": "2629098b-3fd1-32a3-af57-604cd524dcbf",
                                                "text": "Gayly to bourgeon and broadly to grow."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0d931288-c9d4-41c9-b3d0-493599271722",
                                                "sense_id": "2629098b-3fd1-32a3-af57-604cd524dcbf",
                                                "text": "He was much over-dressed, in a gaudy vest of many colors, a blue neckerchief, bedropped gayly with yellow spots, and arranged with a flaunting tie, quite in keeping with the general air of the man."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7640a8a3-1687-40e4-950c-d9ffe9c5838b",
                                                "sense_id": "2629098b-3fd1-32a3-af57-604cd524dcbf",
                                                "text": "In the lightness of my heart I sang catches of songs as my horse gayly bore me along the well-remembered road."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20ad3839-b172-46c7-8e76-eefbe0451b95",
                                                "sense_id": "2629098b-3fd1-32a3-af57-604cd524dcbf",
                                                "text": "Gayly-dressed mavournins and blaring bands stepped lively along Fifth Avenue."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
